    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d168-a2">

                <pb facs="0527" n="469" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg469"/>

                <head>Mr. Burton to Mr. Rice</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 16.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Bogota</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1865-12-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 20, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your two notes of November 24, 1865,
                    relating to the killing of a negro on the wharf at Aspinwall by a sentinel of
                    the United States steamer James Adger, on the 10th ultimo, was received to-day.
                    I will thank you to inquire into and inform me as fully as practicable of the
                    facts connected with the occurrence.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ALLAN A. BURTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>F. W. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rice</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >United States Consul, Aspinwall</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
